    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is neutral or negative (0.00) and model shows persistent overestimation.",
    "Reduce forecast peaks by 5-10% after a spike, especially if sentiment remains flat or negative.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast deviates >10% from recent 7-day average, correct toward that average.",
    "Avoid over-optimism in early forecast periods (e.g., first 5 days of 30d window) — sentiment-driven corrections should be applied early.",
    "If sentiment history shows a single positive signal (0.25), reduce forecast by 3-5% to avoid overreaction.",
    "For long-term (30d) forecasts, cap upward momentum after 10-15 days to prevent overshoots in bullish sentiment."
